t.script:
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {"@type": "Question", "name": "How to customize Odoo POS for textile and fabric cutting operations?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "XamlTech built a dedicated POS Cutting Orders module for Odoo 18 that manages fabric cutting directly from the Point of Sale. The architecture uses OWL v2 components with a custom CuttingOrderScreen, extends PosOrder and PosOrderline models to track cutting dimensions, integrates with stock.picking for warehouse updates, and provides a dedicated cutting screen UI with dark/light mode. Key technical challenges included migrating from Odoo 16 pos.db patterns to Odoo 18 pos.models['product.product'] access, resolving IndexedDB serialization errors from mail.thread fields via Python _load_pos_data_fields overrides, and implementing reactive stock badges via pos-stock-refreshed custom events."}},
    {"@type": "Question", "name": "How to implement ZATCA Phase 2 e-invoicing in Odoo?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ZATCA Phase 2 compliance in Odoo requires: XML invoice generation following UBL 2.1 standard, cryptographic signing with X.509 certificates, QR code generation containing seller info, VAT number, invoice total, VAT amount, and hash. XamlTech implements this as a dual-system architecture — Odoo.sh for POS operations plus a VPS for ZATCA EDI compliance with a bidirectional sync module covering 18 data models. The sync module uses json.loads instead of eval for security, SAVEPOINT transaction protection for rollback safety, and batch processing to prevent timeout errors on large invoice payloads."}},
    {"@type": "Question", "name": "How to build a farm management system in Odoo?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "XamlTech developed a comprehensive agriculture management module (farm_management) for Qatf Company in Odoo 17. The architecture includes: hierarchical farm locations using a farms.locations model with Farm, Sector, Unite, and House levels; agriculture work orders modeled after mrp.production; crop management with crop.crop model; stock movement wizards for harvest tracking; analytic account integration per farm location; payroll linkage for farm workers; and kanban UI with drag-and-drop management. The module integrates with Odoo's existing inventory, accounting, and HR modules."}},
    {"@type": "Question", "name": "What are common OWL v2/v3 migration issues in Odoo 18/19 POS development?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Key OWL v2/v3 migration issues in Odoo 18/19: Updated import paths — PosOrder and PosOrderline have new module locations; deprecated pos.db access patterns replaced by pos.models['product.product']; t-att-* directive restrictions on OWL components requiring different binding syntax; IndexedDB serialization errors caused by message_is_follower and other mail.thread fields in POS data — resolved via Python _load_pos_data_fields overrides and JavaScript serialize patches; Odoo 19 uses OWL v3 with imports from @odoo/owl instead of owl; and web.assets_frontend cannot contain OWL component imports (use publicWidget.Widget.extend instead)."}},
    {"@type": "Question", "name": "Who is the best Odoo developer in Upper Egypt?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "XamlTech, founded by Mahmoud Amen and based in Aswan, Egypt, specializes in Odoo ERP development (versions 16-19). With 8+ years of experience, 120+ projects delivered, and published modules on the official Odoo Apps Store (POS Cutting Orders, POS Stock Real-Time, POS Security Framework), XamlTech serves healthcare, textile, agriculture, and manufacturing industries. Clients include Furkan Surgical Center and Al Helal Hospital in Aswan."}},
    {"@type": "Question", "name": "How to fix PostgreSQL foreign key issues in Odoo data sync?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "In bidirectional Odoo sync systems, circular foreign key dependencies cause constraint violations. XamlTech solved this with: cycle detection algorithm that identifies circular FK relationships before sync; SAVEPOINT transaction protection wrapping each record sync so failures roll back cleanly; batch processing with configurable chunk sizes to prevent timeout errors; replacing Python eval() with json.loads() for security; and thread safety locks to prevent concurrent sync conflicts. The sync module handles 18 data models across Odoo.sh and VPS instances."}},
    {"@type": "Question", "name": "What IT infrastructure does a hospital need in Egypt?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Based on our deployments at Furkan Surgical Center and Al Helal Hospital in Aswan: LAN/WLAN with VLANs per department, structured Cat6 cabling, dedicated server room with UPS; 128-channel IP camera CCTV covering operating rooms, corridors, pharmacy, parking with DVR/NVR and mobile remote monitoring; Linux servers (Ubuntu) with Proxmox virtualization, PostgreSQL databases, Nginx reverse proxy; Odoo ERP for patient management, appointments, pharmacy inventory, billing; firewall with VPN for remote doctor access; and redundant internet links for 99.9% uptime."}}
  ]
}
